From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 09:35:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Release 0.3.1

Documentation only. The library is byte-for-byte the code that 0.3.0 shipped:
no behaviour change, no public API change, no dependency change.

It exists for one line of metadata. A documentation site is built from the
repository, but the link a reader follows from PyPI comes from the package that
was uploaded, and 0.3.0's says `#readme`. There is no way to correct that
without publishing a version.

Also fixes the 0.2.0 link at the foot of CHANGELOG.md, which pointed at
`github.comit`.
